-We identified \emph{normalization-induced co-adaptation} as the root cause of MoE routing collapse on time series foundation models. Seven causal controls---including opposite entropy trajectories on identical data (Figure~\ref{fig:causal_contrast})---isolate the mechanism, and a mutual-information decomposition predicts where it applies ($\rho{=}{-}0.88$, $n{=}9$). \textbf{RR-MoA} breaks the collapse by routing on raw, pre-normalization input, achieving \textbf{54/54 wins} and a Frozen Paradox where frozen adapters outperform full fine-tuning by $12$--$79\%$. A dual-stream extension, \textbf{Residual-IA\textsuperscript{+}}, matches or beats DLinear on \textbf{108/123 cells} across six backbones.
+We identified \emph{normalization-induced co-adaptation} as the root cause of MoE routing collapse on time series foundation models. Seven causal controls---including opposite entropy trajectories on identical data (Figure~\ref{fig:causal_contrast})---isolate the mechanism, and a mutual-information decomposition predicts where it applies ($\rho{=}{-}0.88$, $n{=}9$). \textbf{RR-MoA} breaks the collapse by routing on raw, pre-normalization input, achieving \textbf{54/54 wins} and a Frozen Paradox where frozen adapters outperform full fine-tuning by $12$--$79\%$. A dual-stream extension, \textbf{Residual-IA\textsuperscript{+}}, matches or beats DLinear on \textbf{108/123 cells} across six backbones---with $15/16$ losses at $H{\geq}192$ and $\mathbf{100\%}$ on Timer-XL and Moirai-MoE.

